{#
  Inline SVG icons for the public marketing page.

  lucide-react is a React component library, so it is unreachable from Twig.
  This is the same path data, lifted verbatim from
  node_modules/lucide-react/dist/esm/icons/*.js (ISC licensed) and wrapped in
  lucide's own attribute set — 24x24 viewBox, currentColor stroke, stroke-width
  2, round caps and joins — so these sit on exactly the same optical grid as the
  icons the app itself draws.

  Usage:
      {% from 'marketing/_icons.html.twig' import icon %}
      {{ icon('truck', 20, 'text-primary') }}

  viewBox stays 24x24 while width/height scale, which is what keeps stroke
  weight proportional. For icons rendered above ~32px pass strokeWidth=1.5, or
  the line looks heavy.

  Every icon is decorative: it is always paired with visible text, so it carries
  aria-hidden="true" (keeps it out of the accessibility tree) and
  focusable="false" (keeps it out of the tab order in legacy Edge/IE). The macro
  deliberately offers no way to label the SVG itself — if an icon is ever the
  only content of a link or button, put aria-label on that link or button.

  An unknown name renders an empty <svg> in prod and throws under
  strict_variables in dev, which is where a typo should surface.
#}
{% macro icon(name, size = 24, class = '', strokeWidth = 2) %}
